# Q: what does a brown-out actually do, rank by rank — and does the bank buy the base time?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --detection-demo --probe tools/probe/power.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/power.txt
#
# The detection fixture's base, whose ledger the radar and the emplacement work was built
# against. The brown-out is §4's third leg: a shortfall drains the stockpile first, the bank
# pays, and only when the bank cannot cover a tick's deficit does the shed land — detection
# first, then the guns, then production.
#
#   - the healthy line: everything on.
#   - the strike: the plant off the map, the bank emptied (`power drain`), and the
#     readings show the shed landing rank by rank — the dish dark, the gun silenced.
#   - `range` on the emplacement says zero while it is silenced — the same answer the
#     dark radar's coverage gives.

power 0
range 504

# --- the strike: the plant off the map, the bank emptied -------------------------------
strike PowerPlant
power drain
tick 2
power 0
range 504
